<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos</h1><p class="st-meta">1185 CE – 1479 CE · capital Cephalonia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ionian island county ruled by the Orsini and Tocco families for three centuries, a link between Italy, the Frankish Morea and Epirus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1185 the Norman admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaritus-of-brindisi">Margaritus of Brindisi</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-sicily">William II of Sicily</a>. By about 1195 the islands were held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-orsini">Matthew Orsini</a>, of an Apulian family, who founded a hereditary lordship and placed himself in turn under the protection of the Pope, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts ruled a Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> population through Italian and Greek officials, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> alongside the Orthodox clergy. The Orsini intermarried with the rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-epirus">Despotate of Epirus</a> and later acquired it. In 1357 the county passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-i-tocco">Leonardo I Tocco</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-i-tocco">Carlo I Tocco</a> extended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tocco-family">Tocco</a> power to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> and Arta.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-iii-tocco">Leonardo III Tocco</a> lost his mainland lands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and in 1479 the islands as well, fleeing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> in 1485 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> in 1500, making them part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-ionian-islands">Venetian Ionian Islands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-palatine-of-cephalonia-and-zakynthos.jpg" alt="County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos" width="320" height="358"><figcaption>Image: Кардам · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:County_palatine_of_Cephalonia_and_Zakynthos.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1185 CE – 1479 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cephalonia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Matthew Orsini, Carlo I Tocco, Leonardo III Tocco</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Medieval Greek, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Cephalonia, Orsini and Tocco county</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1332&amp;focus=county-palatine-of-cephalonia-and-zakynthos" aria-label="County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5195 812 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5515 1068L5333 1064M5515 1068L5530 1071M5515 1068L5349 976M5515 1068L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5333 1064h0M5530 1071h0M5349 976h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5515 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5515 1068h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1332&amp;focus=county-palatine-of-cephalonia-and-zakynthos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

